# ── Organizer-supplied material ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# brief/ held the original problem-statement materials (internal working files, not published).
# This material belongs to the organizers. Redistributing it in a PUBLIC
# submission repository is Mehul's call, not an agent's — so the reversible
# default is to ignore it. It stays on disk and stays readable by both agents;
# it just does not ship. To include it, delete these two lines and record the
# decision in the internal working notes.
brief/

# ── Bulky run artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# results/ keeps small, auditable evidence (JSON, CSV, MD) — those are tracked,
# because the truthfulness rule requires cited numbers to be reproducible from a
# tracked file. Large captures and recordings are not.
results/**/*.ndjson
results/**/*.jsonl
results/**/*.zip
results/**/*.tar.gz
*.mov
*.mp4
*.webm
# Exception: the challenge submission requires a publicly accessible demo video.
!demo/walnut-rewind-demo.mp4

